THIRD-PARTY DATA

The MIT terms above cover this repository's own code and prose. Two of the
datasets the cases are built on are other people's work, published under their
own terms, and are attributed here because that is a condition of using them —
not merely a courtesy.

**Our World in Data** — CO2 and Greenhouse Gas Emissions, and education
expenditure as a share of GDP. Licensed CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Source:
https://ourworldindata.org. Neither dataset is redistributed in this
repository; `scripts/load_cases.py` and `scripts/setup_workspace.py` take a CSV
you download yourself, which is also why Free Edition's restricted outbound
network does not break the setup.

**Bickel, Hammel & O'Connell (1975)**, "Sex Bias in Graduate Admissions: Data
from Berkeley", *Science* 187(4175). The six-department admissions table is
transcribed in `src/prove_it/case_data.py` — twelve published cells, checked
against the paper and against R's `datasets::UCBAdmissions` by
`tests/test_case_data.py`. It is quoted as published data for teaching, with
the source named on the case card in the app itself.

**`student_scores` is synthetic.** It is generated from a fixed seed by
`notebooks/01_generate_data.py`, contains no real pupils, and is labelled as
synthetic wherever it appears on screen. No real personal data of any kind is
used anywhere in this project.
